    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_964a160c",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The group of friends laughing is mapped to the person named 'Mohammad' who is being called back.",
      "description": "The top text 'wait, mohammad come back!!' implies that the person named Mohammad is the subject of the group's laughter, and the visual of the laughing group is mapped onto this textual reference. The group's laughter is being projected as the reaction to Mohammad, even though he is not visually present. The text explicitly names 'Mohammad', creating an analogical mapping between the group's reaction (visual) and the named individual (textual).",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
